<div class="page-head">
  <div>
    <div class="eyebrow">Draft · first word goes out with your next send after launch</div>
    <h1>Your first game <span class="badge badge-amber">Draft</span></h1>
  </div>
  <div class="actions">
    <%= button_to "Launch game", account_publication_game_launch_path(publication_id: @publication.id, game_id: game.id),
          method: :post, class: "btn btn-primary btn-small",
          form: { data: { turbo_confirm: "Launch this game? Words lock into their reveal order. The first goes out with your next send." } } %>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>What launch does</h2>
  <p class="small muted">Launching locks these <%= game.pool_size %> words into the reveal order below.
    A new word goes live automatically each time you send. The first click of each issue draws it.
    Nothing happens between sends.</p>
  <p class="small muted">After this first launch, games run continuously. When one ends, the next
    starts on its own, and you can always adjust it here beforehand. Prizes and the sponsor live on
    the Sponsors &amp; Prizes tab and apply to every game.</p>
</div>

<div style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
  <%= render "word_list", game: game %>
</div>
